      "thm:inverse-count-baseline-upper",
      "thm:common-marginal-converse"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "The lower inequality is (39) in \\(\\texttt{thm:common-marginal-converse}\\).  The baseline estimator in \\(\\texttt{thm:inverse-count-baseline-upper}\\) gives\n\\[\nR_\\epsilon(n,m,2)\\le C_\\epsilon\\left\\{\\frac1n+\\frac4{(n+m)^2}\\right\\}\n\\le\\frac{5C_\\epsilon}{n},\n\\]\nbecause \\(n+m\\ge n\\ge1\\) implies \\((n+m)^{-2}\\le n^{-1}\\).  This includes null cells and every finite or infinite auxiliary-sample regime.",
